00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:04.000
Nicole: What exactly is a cyber
security incident response plan?

00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:09.530
A cyber security incident plan consists
of instructions on how to respond to and

00:00:09.530 --> 00:00:12.030
recover from network security incidents.

00:00:12.710 --> 00:00:16.499
Abraham: Incident plans may be drawn
up to address issues such as malware

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:21.220
detection, data theft and service
outages, but it also should include

00:00:21.250 --> 00:00:25.020
all areas as cyber attacks can
affect any part of an organisation.

00:00:25.890 --> 00:00:29.800
So, when is a cyber security
incident response plan used?

00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:34.649
Nicole: As we have previously mentioned
every organisation whether large or small

00:00:34.699 --> 00:00:39.740
should have a Cyber Security Incident
Response Plan or IR and this usually

00:00:39.740 --> 00:00:42.080
comes into play when a breach is detected.

00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:46.910
It can also help to protect a system
by planning for backups to secure data,

00:00:47.179 --> 00:00:51.949
security alerts to detect any malicious
activity and efficient patch management.

00:00:52.539 --> 00:00:56.679
Identity and access management should
be used to avoid insider threats.

00:00:57.659 --> 00:01:02.030
Abraham: Incident response planning can
protect an organisations reputation by

00:01:02.030 --> 00:01:03.960
helping to show that they are prepared.

00:01:04.719 --> 00:01:09.019
It can also be a more cost-effective way
of handling cyber security as breaches

00:01:09.020 --> 00:01:14.339
can be expensive due to loss of data,
downtime of systems, costs involved with

00:01:14.339 --> 00:01:16.310
investigating and restoring systems.

00:01:16.780 --> 00:01:19.869
Nicole: Having an incident response
plan is an important part of the

00:01:19.870 --> 00:01:21.720
whole cyber security process.

00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:25.780
It can help set out the role that
everyone should play and the processes

00:01:25.780 --> 00:01:29.640
that should be followed at all
times and not just during an attack.

00:01:30.359 --> 00:01:31.483
Abraham: A plan should consist of a
series of actions to follow but should

00:01:31.483 --> 00:01:31.490
also provide a checklist approach so
that actions are consistent across

00:01:31.490 --> 00:01:31.509
all areas appropriate to the plan.

